# Exclude everything, then let back in only what the image copies.
#
# The working directory is ~3.7 GB -- the OSM graph, the census extracts, the
# virtualenv, the caches. The image needs 14 MB of it. Without this the build
# context alone is the whole thing, sent to the daemon before the first
# instruction runs, and a deploy from a clean clone would still drag in
# anything a build step happened to produce.
*

!replays/
!src/
!deploy/
!Dockerfile

# Nothing under src/ is served except the dashboard; the simulator and the
# agent produced these recordings and are not needed to play them back.
src/*
!src/viz/

# Belt and braces: never ship credentials or fixtures even if a rule above
# were loosened later.
**/.env
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
fixtures/
.venv/
